On Mon, Nov 22, 2010 at 01:59:22PM -0800, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> On Mon, Nov 22, 2010 at 01:54:37PM -0800, Matt Arnold wrote:
> > Everyone please keep in mind the poll is not "which
> > languages/frameworks do you think other people should program
> > jbovlaste2 in", it's which ones you are committing to help with. I
> > am not very confident that an anonymous poll will prove accurate
> > when the time comes to pay up with our time.
> 
> I am anti-confident; my confidence in people in this community
> paying with their time has been thoroughly eroded over the years.
> 
> I just wanted to know what to *avoid*.  :)  In particular, I like
> weblocks, and wanted to know how stupid it would be to write
> something in that.
> 

It is interesting to me that the Lojban community managed to publish
a book, write a parser, and create a complete-ish specification for
the language--yet this sentiment of not having support, help,
encourgagement, or focus is commonly expressed.

Robin, is your expectation of what people will accomplish out of line?
Has the community changed?  Did it used to be better?

I'm curious as to what is going on, as I don't quite see us having
the skills and committement to publish a book, but some of us did
that anyway.

